<% sweep = Lab::SWEEPS.fetch("reach_cap128") %>
<% grid = sweep.fetch(:param_grid) %>
<% seeds = sweep.fetch(:seeds) %>
<% epochs = number_with_delimiter sweep.fetch(:epochs), delimiter: " " %>
<% rate_exponent = -Math.log2(Lab::EMERGENT_MUTATION_RATE).round %>
<% record_url = "https://github.com/hanscanonico/life_simulator/blob/main/docs/design_record.md" %>
<% constants = Lab::ReachCap128Reading %>

<h2>Question</h2>
<p>
  <%= link_to "Emergence peaks at an intermediate reach", finding_path("emergence-peaks-at-intermediate-reach") %>
  found, on tapes held at 64 bytes, that a replicator arises most often when a cell reaches
  about four cells away. Every rung-4 experiment runs instead on tapes that can grow, and starts
  from emerged worlds of that kind, of which the lab had few: the host–parasite sweep's
  economy-off control at cap 128 emerged in 11 of its 270 worlds, at radius 1. DESIGN §1.3
  sweep 14 asks two things at once: <strong>does the reach effect carry to growable tapes, and
  does it give rung 4 a pool of parents?</strong>
</p>

<h2>Method</h2>
<p>
  The control's world to the byte — a <%= grid.fetch("width").first %>×<%= grid.fetch("height").first %>
  torus, tapes of <%= grid.fetch("tape_len").first %> bytes free to grow to
  <%= grid.fetch("max_tape_len").first %>, the emergent mutation rate
  <span class="mono">2<sup>-<%= rate_exponent %></sup></span>, the economy off — at radius
  <%= constants::TREATMENT_RADIUS %>, with <span class="mono">lineage_rule = oriented</span>,
  which changes no byte of a world. Seeds <%= seeds.first %>–<%= seeds.last %>, the control's,
  <%= epochs %> epochs, <%= seeds.size %> runs. Radius changes the world, so these are new
  worlds; the control is the host–parasite sweep's own runs at radius 1, a historical arm the
  engine's determinism makes comparable.
</p>
<p>
  The reading is <strong>pre-registered</strong>, with every number fixed before a run was
  read: <%= link_to "docs/design_record.md", record_url %>, 2026-10-01, "Does the reach effect
  carry to growable tapes?". Emergence is read identically in both arms off the stored worlds:
  a run is emerged where it has a confirmed emergence epoch and the orientation-aware census of
  some world it kept, from that epoch on, reads <span class="mono">replicator_share</span> of at
  least <%= percent_value constants::MIN_SHARE %>. A run counts once the readings pass has read
  every world it kept. <strong>H-reach128</strong>: radius <%= constants::TREATMENT_RADIUS %>
  emerges more often than the control, one one-sided Fisher exact test at
  p &lt; <%= constants::LEVEL %>. Everything else on this page is descriptive.
</p>

<% reading = @show.reach_cap128 %>
<h2>Result</h2>
<% if reading&.any? %>
  <% treatment = reading.treatment %>
  <% control = reading.control %>
  <p id="reach-cap128-finding-claim">
    <span class="badge <%= reading.comparison.badge_class %>">H-reach128 <%= reading.comparison.outcome_label %></span>
    <strong><%= reading.claim_sentence %></strong>
    <% if reading.comparison.testable? %>
      One-sided Fisher exact test, p = <%= p_value_text reading.p_value %>.
    <% end %>
    On one world: a 128×128 torus, tapes of 64 bytes growing to 128,
    <span class="mono">2<sup>-<%= rate_exponent %></sup></span>, <%= epochs %> epochs.
  </p>
  <% if reading.interim? %>
    <p>Not every run of the two arms has finished and been read, so this reading is interim.</p>
  <% end %>
  <p class="text-sm text-muted">
    Every count on this page is read from the stored runs at render time, through the same
    reading <%= link_to "the sweep page", experiment_path("reach-cap128", anchor: "reach-cap128-reading") %>
    draws. Before the reading went final, a readings-pass bug left one stored world of each of
    two radius-4 runs unread, holding it interim at 117 of 268 counted; once it was fixed (#299)
    and the worlds read, both runs read as emerged.
  </p>

  <%= render "experiments/reach_cap128_reading", reading: reading.report %>

  <% if treatment.emerged.positive? && control.emerged.positive? %>
    <h2 class="mt-6">The replicators that arose</h2>
    <p id="reach-cap128-finding-secondaries">
      Descriptive, over the emerged runs, and deciding nothing. The median emergence epoch is
      <%= number_with_delimiter treatment.median_emergence_epoch, delimiter: " " %> at radius <%= constants::TREATMENT_RADIUS %>
      and <%= number_with_delimiter control.median_emergence_epoch, delimiter: " " %> in the control. The median terminal
      share of the world replicators hold is <%= percent_value treatment.median_terminal_share %>
      and <%= percent_value control.median_terminal_share %>. The dominant replicator's median
      length is <%= metric_value treatment.median_raw_len %> and
      <%= metric_value control.median_raw_len %> bytes, so the tapes use the room they were
      given, and its median instruction count is <%= metric_value treatment.median_instruction_count %>
      and <%= metric_value control.median_instruction_count %>. The dominant tape of the terminal
      world self-replicates in <%= treatment.self_replicating_dominant %> of
      <%= treatment.emerged %> emerged runs and <%= control.self_replicating_dominant %> of
      <%= control.emerged %>.
    </p>
  <% end %>

  <h2>A pool of parents</h2>
  <p id="reach-cap128-finding-parents">
    An eligible parent is an emerged world whose terminal stored world reads a share of at least
    <%= percent_value constants::PARENT_SHARE %>. Radius <%= constants::TREATMENT_RADIUS %> gives
    <%= treatment.eligible_parents %> of them, against <%= control.eligible_parents %> in the
    control, every one with tapes that have room to grow. The pool is counted here and nothing
    more: no later sweep's parent rule is locked by this reading, and a sweep that starts from
    these worlds states its own.
  </p>
<% else %>
  <p class="text-muted">
    No run of <%= link_to "the sweep", experiment_path("reach-cap128") %> is in this database,
    so there is no arm to read here. This page reads the arms at render time and states the
    claim from them.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>How it reads against sweep 13</h2>
<p>
  On fixed 64-byte tapes,
  <%= link_to "sweep 13", finding_path("emergence-peaks-at-intermediate-reach") %> read radius 4
  at 16 of 90 against radius 1's 4 of 90, four times the rate. On growable tapes the effect is
  larger. That is a comparison of two sweeps, not a test: they read emergence on different
  instruments (sweep 13 on live samples, this one on stored worlds), on different seeds and
  under different lineage rules, so nothing here says that room to grow is what made the
  difference.
</p>

<h2>What is not claimed</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>One world, one reach against one.</strong> Every run is 128×128, at one mutation
    rate, one cap of 128 bytes and a budget of <%= epochs %> epochs, and only radius 4 was run
    against the control's radius 1. Where the peak sits on growable tapes is untested.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>A historical control.</strong> The control ran in September under the
    <span class="mono">aligned</span> lineage rule and an older engine build; neither moves a
    byte of a world, so its runs are the runs it would be today, but they were not run beside
    this sweep.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Rate or speed.</strong> A difference inside <%= epochs %> epochs can be a difference
    in how soon a replicator arises rather than whether it does.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>No mechanism.</strong> Nothing here says why a reach of 4 helps more on growable
    tapes than the locality finding saw on fixed ones.
  </li>
</ul>
